-- KNOWN LEAK (inner-abstraction family, DEFERRED to the slice after rung 2):
-- TYPECHECKS today, the type LIES. `helper` is a POINT-FREE 0-arg binding whose
-- body is a lambda performing the caller-supplied residual `e`. It is accepted
-- (`forall a. Suspension U64 U64 U64 a -> U64`) even though the eta-equivalent
-- explicit-param form `helper g = run g 0` is correctly REJECTED. Cause:
-- typeEquationWith's zero-parameter branch never collects caller-roots, and the
-- lambda body absorbs the residual. Same family as launder-leak-inner-lambda;
-- needs the inner-abstraction propagation fix (which must also extend root
-- collection to the 0-arg branch), NOT rung-2's provenance rule.
-- See docs/superpowers/2026-07-02-lambda-effect-laundering-note.md
helper : Suspension U64 U64 U64 (row e) -> U64
helper = \ g -> run g 0
main : U64
main = 0
